summary:
- topic: New Board Member and Meeting Procedures
  text: The board welcomed new member Adrian Dowling, conducted a land acknowledgement,
    and introduced a new 'Board Communications' segment for members to share updates
    and commendations from their school visits and event attendance.
- topic: Student Reports and Recognitions
  text: The student representative reported on activities across the district's schools.
    The board then honored a group of students for achieving All-State Music honors
    and recognized numerous senior student-athletes named to the SMAA All-Academic
    and All-Citizenship teams.
- topic: Superintendent's Report
  text: Superintendent Matheney reported that chronic student absenteeism has improved
    by 3% district-wide, all federal ESSER relief funds were successfully spent, and
    community generosity for the 'Season of Giving' has been strong.
- topic: Adult Education Program Update
  text: Director Erin Krivicky detailed the Adult Education program's rapid growth,
    particularly in ESOL classes. She highlighted the program's heavy reliance on
    unstable grant funding and made the case for increased, sustainable local budget
    support to match the model used by other districts.
- topic: K-4 Math Curriculum Proposal
  text: Director Erica Mazzeo presented the curriculum committee's recommendation
    to adopt the HMH 'Into Math' program for grades K-4. The proposal follows an in-depth
    review process and includes a five-year implementation plan with an estimated
    cost of around $250,000.
- topic: Mental and Behavioral Health Initiatives
  text: Director Erika Boulware provided an update on the district's mental health
    landscape, highlighting the proactive work of staff and engagement with support
    organizations. She also announced a partnership with SoPo Unite to apply for a
    $500,000 opioid settlement grant to enhance services.
- topic: Public Comment on Athletic Fields
  text: A citizen representing a local advocacy group spoke against the use of artificial
    turf for the high school athletic fields, citing health and environmental research.
    The group requested to be included in the board's upcoming study of the issue.
- topic: Board Business and Committee Reports
  text: The board approved the consent agenda and the 2025 meeting calendar. Committee
    reports included a stable financial outlook from the Finance Committee and a review
    of policy updates from the Policy Committee.
